<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tribhuwana Wijayatunggadewi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1328">1328</a>–<a href="/years/1350">1350</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Dyah Gitarja, Gitarja, Tribhuwannottunggadewi Jayawishnuwardhani, Dyah Tya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tribhuwana Wijayatunggadewi, also known as Dyah Gitarja, was a Javanese queen regnant and the third monarch of the Majapahit empire, reigning from 1328 to 1350. A daughter of the empire's founder, Kertarajasa Jayawardhana, and his principal wife Gayatri, she had been confined in the palace by her half-brother King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayanegara">Jayanegara</a>, and came to the throne at her mother's order after he was murdered in 1328. In 1331 she led the army against rebels in Sadeng and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keta">Keta</a>, and in 1334 she made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gajah-mada">Gajah Mada</a> her prime minister; with him she pursued a great expansion of the empire, which conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> in 1343. On her mother's death in 1350 she abdicated in favour of her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayam-wuruk">Hayam Wuruk</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tribhuwana-wijayatunggadewi.jpg" alt="Tribhuwana Wijayatunggadewi" width="330" height="605" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parvati_Majapahit_1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
